From b896f8ad686dc5111640744f5265a84cb3f30660 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:52:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Desktop poll cost: revalidate kanban annotation on
 unchanged inputs, cache gateway platforms/manifest names/status session rows
 on file signatures

laptop-1 profile (t_01a199a0a5d38255 / t_01a19d0bcab45558): the kanban annotation refreshed every ~3 s because the
counts TTL expired while no board content moved (3 of 60 polls saw a revision change), and every /api/status poll
reloaded the gateway config (re-parsing ~27 bundled manifests) and re-read state.db for the active-session count.

- kanban_session_activity: past the TTL, counts and attention verdicts read under an unchanged, revalidatable
  fingerprint are re-served inline (no refresh thread), bounded by _COUNTS_MAX_AGE_S / _ATTENTION_MAX_AGE_S for
  time-derived states; stat-keyed boards count only once their mtime settled.
- kanban_activity_revision: memoize the trigger-coverage check on schema_version.
- gateway/config: memoize bundled manifest names on file signature.
- web_server_gateway: connected platforms kept on config/.env/gateway.json/managed signatures + env + home (60 s max age).
- web_routers/status: active-session rows kept on settled state.db/-wal signatures; window applied per call.

Tests RED first; each cache key component mutation-checked.
